description: A program corpus that tests the language, not one lane's mechanism, should run on both the GC and llvm lanes, so neither covers a program the other skips. A test of one lane's mechanism gets a twin in the other lane instead: refusals through a `;; refuse-llvm:` header, WasmGC's poly placeholders through corpus/poly.
 
 Plan:
 1. The llvm lane runs the GC lane's program corpora through checks/common-corpora.sh (row P13.9).
 2. The GC-only suites get llvm twins (P13.10-P13.14): refusals, core tests, legmacs' suites, legmacs parity, multimethods.
 3. To match native, llvm needs runtime twins for eval and namespaces, regex Unicode classes, overflow-checked boxed arithmetic, foreign error printing, bound-fn frames, multimethods and rooted natives (alter-var-root of a native fn).
 
 Acceptance: P13.9-P13.14, P12.3a, P12.3b, P12.31 and the llvm corpora pass on the branch; rows and baseline recorded through checks/workflow.mk.
 
 Refs git-issue:f7fff20 (ex-message on llvm), git-issue:646deae (common runtime core).
